    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d276">

                <pb facs="0464" n="362" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg362"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.113/255</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Swedish Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Boström</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Castle</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-02-28">February 28,
                        1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Castle</hi>: Referring to our
                    conversation on February 9th about the Swedish Government’s willingness to
                    cooperate with the United States Government with a view to a concerted action
                    between the arms-producing countries in a certain situation, I beg to <pb
                        facs="0465" n="363" xml:id="pg363"/> inform you that I have now received a
                    telegram from my Government to the effect that my assumption was correct that it
                    would be willing to cooperate with your and other interested Governments in the
                    direction outlined in the resolution now before Congress.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Boström</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
